2:T2e55,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Batteriq an authorised EcoFlow dealer in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Batteriq is Kenya's officially appointed EcoFlow distributor. Every product we sell is 100% genuine, sourced directly from EcoFlow, and comes with the full official EcoFlow international warranty. As an authorised dealer, we also provide EcoFlow-certified after-sales support, spare parts, and warranty claim processing directly in Kenya."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is Batteriq located?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Batteriq is based in Nairobi, Kenya. We serve customers across all 47 counties with nationwide courier delivery. For Nairobi customers, we offer same-day and next-day delivery options."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Batteriq sell Bluetti products as an authorised dealer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Batteriq stocks and sells Bluetti power stations in Kenya. For Bluetti-specific warranty and authorisation queries, please contact us directly and we will advise on the appropriate support channel."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to charge an EcoFlow power station?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Charging time depends on the model and charging method: • EcoFlow DELTA Pro: ~1.9 hours via AC wall charging (2900W input) • EcoFlow DELTA 2: ~1.3 hours via AC wall charging (1200W input) • EcoFlow RIVER 2: ~60 minutes via AC wall charging (360W input) • EcoFlow RIVER 3: ~60 minutes via AC wall charging Solar charging times vary depending on panel wattage and sunlight conditions. EcoFlow's X-Stream fast charging technology charges most models to 80% in under 1 hour."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use an EcoFlow power station while it is charging?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. All EcoFlow power stations support simultaneous charging and discharging — called \"pass-through charging\". You can power your devices while the unit is plugged in and charging. This is particularly useful as a UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply) for home offices and essential equipment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many times can I charge and discharge an EcoFlow battery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"EcoFlow power stations use LFP (Lithium Iron Phosphate) battery chemistry, which is rated for: • 3,500+ charge cycles to 80% capacity • This equates to approximately 10 years of daily use After 3,500 cycles, the battery retains at least 80% of its original capacity — it does not suddenly fail. LFP chemistry is also significantly safer and more stable than traditional lithium-ion batteries."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I leave my EcoFlow power station plugged in all the time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. EcoFlow power stations are designed to be left plugged in continuously. The Battery Management System (BMS) automatically stops charging when the battery reaches 100% and manages optimal charging cycles to extend battery life. For long-term storage (more than 3 months), EcoFlow recommends storing the unit at 30–60% charge in a cool, dry location."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What appliances can an EcoFlow DELTA Pro power?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The EcoFlow DELTA Pro (3600Wh, 3600W AC output) can power: • Refrigerator (150W) — 15+ hours • Television (100W) — 24+ hours • Laptop (60W) — 40+ hours • LED lights (10W) — multiple days • CPAP machine — 4+ nights • Electric kettle (1500W) — multiple uses • Power tools (intermittent use) For appliances with motors (fridge, AC), always check the surge wattage. The DELTA Pro handles surges up to 7200W."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does EcoFlow work as a UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. EcoFlow RIVER 3 series and DELTA 3 series feature a 10ms UPS switchover time — faster than most household UPS units. This means connected devices experience no interruption during a power outage. The EcoFlow RIVER 3 (UPS) is specifically designed for this use case with a 10ms response time, making it ideal for routers, NAS drives, CCTV systems, and sensitive electronics."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I expand the capacity of my EcoFlow power station?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Several EcoFlow models support extra battery expansion: • DELTA Pro: expandable to 10.8kWh with extra batteries • DELTA 2: expandable to 2kWh with one extra battery • DELTA 2 Max: expandable to 4kWh • DELTA 3 / DELTA 3 Plus: expandable with dedicated extra batteries • RIVER 3 / RIVER 3 Plus: expandable with EB300/EB600 extra batteries All compatible extra batteries are available from Batteriq."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which EcoFlow solar panels are compatible with which power stations?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All EcoFlow portable solar panels (MC4 connector) are compatible with all EcoFlow power stations. The key consideration is total wattage: • RIVER 2 / RIVER 3: max 110W solar input • DELTA 2: max 500W solar input • DELTA 2 Max: max 1000W solar input • DELTA Pro: max 1600W solar input • DELTA Pro 3: max 2600W solar input You can chain multiple panels to reach the max input. All EcoFlow panels use the standard MC4 connector."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much power will I generate from EcoFlow solar panels in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Kenya has excellent solar irradiance — Nairobi averages 5.5 peak sun hours per day. Expected daily output: • 100W panel: ~500Wh/day (0.5kWh) • 220W panel: ~1,100Wh/day (1.1kWh) • 400W panel: ~2,200Wh/day (2.2kWh) Actual output depends on panel angle, shading, temperature, and cloud cover. EcoFlow panels are rated at Standard Test Conditions (25°C, 1000W/m²)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are EcoFlow solar panels waterproof?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. EcoFlow portable solar panels carry an IP68 waterproof rating (except the 45W panel which is IP65). IP68 means complete protection against dust and submersion in water up to 1 metre for 30 minutes. This makes them suitable for use during light rain, outdoor camping, and marine environments. Do not use during heavy storms or lightning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use non-EcoFlow solar panels with an EcoFlow power station?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, with conditions. EcoFlow power stations accept solar input via MC4 connectors. Third-party panels work if: • Voltage is within the accepted range (check your specific model's specs) • Current does not exceed the max input current • Total wattage does not exceed the max solar input For guaranteed compatibility and optimal MPPT charging performance, EcoFlow-branded panels are recommended."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does M-Pesa payment work on Batteriq?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"M-Pesa payment on Batteriq is fully automated: 1. Add items to cart and proceed to checkout 2. Enter your details and select \"Pay Now with M-Pesa\" 3. Enter your M-Pesa phone number 4. Click \"Pay\" — you receive an STK Push prompt on your phone within seconds 5. Enter your M-Pesa PIN to confirm 6. Payment is instantly verified and your order is confirmed No need to manually input a transaction code or send a screenshot. The system verifies automatically."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What payment options does Batteriq offer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Batteriq offers three payment options: 1. Pay Now (M-Pesa STK Push) — instant payment during checkout 2. Cash on Delivery — pay in cash when your order arrives 3. M-Pesa on Delivery — our delivery person triggers an M-Pesa prompt to your phone at the doorstep All payment methods are available for all products."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I cancel or modify my order after placing it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can cancel or modify your order within 2 hours of placing it by contacting us on WhatsApp or calling us directly. After 2 hours, if the order has been dispatched, cancellation may not be possible. For M-Pesa payments that have already been processed, refunds are issued within 3–5 business days back to your M-Pesa account."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How fast is delivery in Nairobi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For Nairobi orders: • Orders placed before 12PM: same-day delivery in most cases • Orders placed after 12PM: next-day delivery • Weekends: delivery available Saturday, Sunday by arrangement Delivery within Nairobi typically takes 2–4 hours from dispatch. You will receive a WhatsApp message with tracking information when your order is dispatched."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you deliver outside Nairobi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We deliver nationwide across all 47 counties via trusted courier partners: • Major towns (Mombasa, Kisumu, Nakuru, Eldoret): 1–2 business days • Other counties: 2–5 business days Delivery fees are calculated at checkout based on your location and the weight/size of your order. Large items like the DELTA Pro require special handling."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I track my order?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"After placing your order, you receive an order confirmation email with your order number. You can track your order at any time by visiting batteriq.com/track-order and entering your order number and email address. No account is required. You will also receive WhatsApp updates when your order is confirmed, dispatched, and out for delivery."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the warranty period for EcoFlow products bought from Batteriq?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Batteriq honours the full official EcoFlow warranty: • Power Stations: 24 months (2 years) • Solar Panels: 24 months product warranty + 5-year power output guarantee (≥90% at year 5) • Extra Batteries: 24 months • Accessories & Cables: 24 months • Smart Generators: 24 months Warranty starts from the date of purchase from Batteriq."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I make a warranty claim in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"To make a warranty claim: 1. Register your product at batteriq.com/support/warranty (do this at purchase) 2. Contact Batteriq directly via WhatsApp or email with: - Your warranty registration number - A description of the issue - Photos or video of the fault 3. Our technical team will assess the claim within 48 hours 4. If approved: repair, replacement, or refund as appropriate As the authorised Kenya distributor, all warranty claims are handled locally — you do not need to ship products internationally."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the EcoFlow warranty NOT cover?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The warranty does not cover: • Physical damage from drops, impacts, or mishandling • Water damage beyond the stated IP rating • Damage from incorrect voltage or power surges • Normal wear and tear (scratches, cosmetic marks) • Damage from unauthorised modifications or repairs • Consumable parts (cables, connectors) after 12 months If your product is damaged due to a manufacturing defect, it is covered. If damaged due to misuse, it is not."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to register my product to get warranty support?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We strongly recommend registering your product at batteriq.com/support/warranty as it speeds up any future warranty claims significantly. However, proof of purchase (M-Pesa receipt or order confirmation email) is sufficient to make a warranty claim even without prior registration."}}]}12:{"size":20}
